      "There is a real category of buyer for whom the ideal breaker finder has one control and no instructions, because it will be used rarely and probably by someone who has forgotten how it worked last time. The Southwire 40130S is built for that: plug the transmitter into the outlet, sweep the receiver down the panel, and it indicates the breaker. There is no sensitivity dial to understand and no technique to learn. On standard residential panels the automatic scanning works well, and in our testing it correctly identified circuits on the modern panel with the same reliability as tools costing considerably more. For a homeowner labelling a panel, that is the whole job done without frustration. The GFCI test on the transmitter adds a genuinely useful second function. The limitation is the flip side of the simplicity. When the panel is crowded and the automatic algorithm settles on the wrong sensitivity, there is no way to intervene, and the tool will confidently indicate on more than one breaker with no means of narrowing further. Sub panels showed the same weakness. Priced between the budget tools and the professional ones, it is a good purchase for a normal house and the wrong one for a complicated installation.",
