          Finding which breaker feeds a particular outlet is one of those jobs that sounds trivial and reliably consumes an afternoon. A breaker finder replaces the walk-back-and-forth method with a transmitter in the outlet and a receiver at the panel, and the difference between a good one and a poor one is entirely in how many breakers it thinks are the right one.
